{"seq":1,"mint":"C9","verb":"claim","status":"ok","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-luna","approach":"split","literals":false,"findings":[{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"in `look_path` the returned bytes and the captured `output` are the same value `shown`","clause_quoted":true,"facts":["F9","F16","F28","F32"],"quoted_from":"output","evidence":"    let mut printed = String::new();\n    printed.push_str(&format!(\"==> {path} <==\\n\"));\n    printed.push_str(&shown);\n    if !shown.is_empty() && !shown.ends_with('\\n') {\n        printed.push('\\n');\n    }\n\n    let entry = PendingEntry {\n        kind: ObservationKind::Path,\n        key,\n        label,\n        output: shown,\n        world_root: world.root,\n        world_state: world.state,\n        captured_at: workspace::now_unix(),\n        pattern: String::new(),\n    };\n    let mut buf = pending::load(workspace_dir)?;\n    buf.push(entry);\n    pending::save(workspace_dir, &buf)?;\n\n    Ok(LookOutcome { printed })","why":"The captured entry stores `shown`, while the function returns `printed`, which adds a header and may add a newline; they are not the same value.","quoted":true},{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"`look_grep` is bounded and `look_path` is not","clause_quoted":true,"facts":["F9","F16","F28","F32"],"quoted_from":"output","evidence":"        Some((a, b)) => {\n            if a < 1 || a > b {\n                return Err(workspace::refuse(workspace_dir, \"look\", format!(\"invalid --lines range {a}:{b}\")));\n            }\n            let all: Vec<&str> = contents.lines().collect();\n            let total = all.len();\n            if a > total {\n                (String::new(), format!(\"{path} lines {a}-{b} (file has {total} line(s); nothing in range)\"))\n            } else {\n                let end = b.min(total);\n                (all[a - 1..end].join(\"\\n\"), format!(\"{path} lines {a}-{end}\"))\n            }\n        }","why":"The `look_path` implementation explicitly clamps the requested end line and returns only the selected range, so the assertion that `look_path` is not bounded is incompatible with the captured code.","quoted":true}],"at":1790113169,"cost":0.01628691,"elapsed_ms":106719,"attempts":3,"not_verbatim":0,"literals_refuted":0,"not_a_quantity":0,"kind_off_verb":0,"refuted":0}
